speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I should also like to present a motion on a question of urgent and pressing necessity.
Considering the importance and the seriousness of the referendum on the constitutional future of Quebec;
Considering the need to let Quebeckers entirely free to chose objectively the appropriate structure for their emancipation and their evolution;
Considering that the most elementary justice and simple logic should lead us to put this debate well above the chauvinism and partisanship inherent in electoralism;
Considering that it would be inadmissible for the federal government spokesmen who do not reside in Quebec to campaign directly or indirectly within the province;
Considering finally that it would also be absurd and unfair to have the taxes which are levied among Quebeckers by the federal government used against their very interests;
I move, seconded by the hon. member for Temiscamingue (Mr. Caouette):
That the House order the government to stop Fighting against the growing awareness of Quebeckers concerning their future and consequently to abolish immediately the Tellier committee which has been created to this end.
